Replaced the `operator[]` access with a single `data()`/`size()` load and marked the in-range case as the expected hot path, so the compiler emits one compare plus a pointer add instead of reloading the vector internals.

```cpp
FieldDefinition* MesgDefinition::GetFieldByIndex(const FIT_UINT16 index)
{
    FieldDefinition* const fieldsData = fields.data();
    const auto fieldCount = fields.size();

    if (__builtin_expect(index < fieldCount, 1))
        return fieldsData + index;

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```